From 227506c862e1a5de5be17f59f6f1c45ca75b26e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 10:57:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 134/252] fix(perf): apply ERR-0004 outlier floor and close
 R2-D2 round validity

ERR-0004 (user-approved 2026-09-11): step 6 now marks
|x - median| > max(3 * 1.4826 * MAD, floor) with
floor = max(1 us, 0.02 * median); outlier_ratio > 0.10 -> UNSTABLE is
unchanged and still evaluated before the cv/p95 gate.

aggregate recomputes case statistics, verdicts and ratios directly from the
stored raw sample arrays plus each round's in-run event_timer_rate, so old
rounds can be regraded under the amended protocol without re-measuring.

R2-D2: round_validity now includes affinity_matches_requested and the
recorded round status; gate.consistency/status/status_basis reflect both.
An explicit --allow-superseded-recorded-status flag permits regrading rounds
recorded under an older protocol revision, while all other round-validity
checks (G1/clock/noise/affinity/blocking-case G2) stay enforced.
